       <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,625.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,625.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ARDOVA</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    OPEC+ Ends 1.65m Bpd Voluntary Cut With 188,000 Bpd September Increase\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    OPEC+ has concluded the phased restoration of its 1.65 million barrels per day (bpd) voluntary production cuts introduced in 2023. The September increase applies to Saudi Arabia, Russia, Iraq, Kuwait, Algeria, Kazakhstan and Oman. The United Arab Emirates, which was originally part of the voluntary production restraint, exited OPEC in May.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/opec-ends-165m-bpd-voluntary-cut-with-188000-bpd-september-increase\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Togo, Cameroon Lead Dangote Refinery Export Destinations in July\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Cameroon and Togo emerged as the leading export destinations for refined petroleum products loaded from the Dangote Petroleum Refinery in July 2026. While exports remained active, domestic deliveries accounted for the majority of the refinery's loading operations.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/togo-cameroon-lead-dangote-refinery-export-destinations-in-july\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Truckified Launches Digital Logistics Operations for Nigeria's Petroleum Supply Chain\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Truckified Limited officially launched operations today as a technology-driven logistics and transportation company focused on Nigeria's petroleum and logistics value chain. The company said its entry addresses longstanding challenges in the sector, including delays in truck deployment, poor fleet visibility, and rising transportation costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/truckified-launches-digital-logistics-operations-for-nigerias-petroleum-supply-chain\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    FG Assures Dangote of Dollar Liquidity to Sustain Naira Fuel Sales – Sources\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has assured the Dangote Petroleum Refinery that it will receive adequate foreign exchange to pay for crude oil purchases. The assurance, which was reportedly given during discussions held on Friday, comes as the implementation of the naira-for-crude initiative continues to face significant supply challenges.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fg-assures-dangote-of-dollar-liquidity-to-sustain-naira-fuel-sales-sources\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Fall Over 5% as Trump Pauses Iran Strikes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $83.44 per barrel, down 5.11 per cent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude fell 5.82 per cent to $79.74 per barrel. The sharp decline follows weeks of heightened volatility across the global oil market.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-fall-over-5-as-trump-pauses-iran-strikes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
